From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:24:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Keep tessera.yml up to date and report mistakes in it

Options added by a newer build are written into an existing tessera.yml with their comments, so the file always lists everything that can be set; the previous file is kept as tessera.yml.old. Values of the wrong type, numbers out of range and unknown keys are reported in the console, unknown keys with the closest known one, and fall back to the default instead of being silently ignored. /tessera reload reads the file again and applies the options that can change while the server runs; the others are reported as needing a restart. Which plugins load in compatibility mode never changes after startup.

